cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AM64x Secure Boot Studio
message: If you use this software or refer to it in your work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Celil
    family-names: Aslan
repository-code: https://github.com/celilaslan/am64x-secure-boot-studio
abstract: >-
  A guided desktop application and command-line toolkit for preparing, inspecting
  and verifying secure boot artifacts on Texas Instruments AM64x / AM6442 devices.
  It wraps the official MCU+ SDK signing tools with host-side validation of
  certificate and signing-key identity, device lifecycle matching, and explicit
  separation between host-side results and on-target enforcement.
keywords:
  - secure boot
  - embedded security
  - X.509
  - code signing
  - Texas Instruments
  - AM64x
  - AM243x
  - MCU+ SDK
  - TISCI
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0-alpha33
